// patterns/generated.ts — MACHINE GENERATED, do not hand-edit
//
// Each entry is the pattern's DISTANCE FIELD at 32x32, one character per
// pixel: the distance from that pixel's centre to the terrain-B side, in pixels
// of the 32px tile, quantised to 0.25 px steps (see FIELD_CHARS). Storing the
// field rather than finished levels is what lets the runtime slide the
// transition band toward the cell border or its centre — it just thresholds
// `field + offset` against the pattern's bands.
//
// Flooring the quantisation is deliberate: every band is a multiple of the step,
// so comparisons survive it and offset 0 reproduces the original art exactly.
//
// PROVENANCE — the two are not equally derived:
//
//   square, sharp   computed analytically at 32. Their generators are solved and
//                   verified: Chebyshev and Euclidean distance to the union of
//                   whole A cells reproduced the old 16px art on 47/47 masks with
//                   zero pixels differing. These are true new samples.
//
//   everything else interpolated up from the 16px art, because cornerRounding and
//                   the five noise generators are still unsolved. This is the
//                   same bilinear step the runtime used to do at render time, so
//                   the silhouette is unchanged; measured against square as a
//                   control it costs at most one 16-space quantisation step.
//
// Generator parameters recorded when the 16px art was first baked:
//
//   square   cornerRounding=0.00 (Chebyshev/square 90°), bands=(3.5, 4.5, 5.5, 6.5)
//   sharp    Euclidean metric, bands=(3.5, 4.5, 5.5, 6.5)
//   rounded  cornerRounding=0.55, bands=(3.5, 4.5, 5.5, 6.5)
//   bold     cornerRounding=0.35, bands=(2.5, 3.5, 5.5, 6.5)
//   jagged   cornerRounding=0.15, bands=(3.5, 4.5, 5.5, 6.5), value noise=1.90 scale=4 seed=7
//   gravel   cornerRounding=0.05, bands=(3.5, 4.5, 5.5, 6.5), value noise=1.40 scale=8 seed=23
//   boulder  cornerRounding=0.50, bands=(4.0, 5.0, 6.0, 7.0), value noise=2.10 scale=2 seed=11
//   thorn    cornerRounding=0.00, bands=(3.75, 4.5, 5.0, 6.0), ridged noise=2.00 scale=5 seed=31
//   coast    cornerRounding=0.25, bands=(3.75, 4.75, 5.75, 6.75), fbm noise=2.00 scale=3 seed=5
//   moss     cornerRounding=0.30, bands=(3.5, 4.5, 5.5, 6.5), worley noise=1.80 scale=4 seed=19
//   billow   cornerRounding=0.45, bands=(3.5, 4.5, 5.5, 6.5), billow noise=1.90 scale=3 seed=13
//
// Those band figures are in the OLD 16-space units; PATTERN_BANDS now carries
// them doubled, because a pixel is half as wide.

